  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The federal market for Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services (NAICS 541611) totals $5.6B in obligations for FY2026 to date. There have been 9,506 awards so far, with an average award size of $592K. Obligations fell 50.2% year over year. FY2026 figures are partial because they represent fiscal year to date activity. Looking at the recent fiscal history shows variability: FY21 was $13.3B, FY22 was $12.9B, FY23 was $14.2B, FY24 was $15B, and FY25 was $11.3B. The drop to $5.6B in FY26 to date represents the current-year total reported so far. On the buyer side, Department of Defense and Department of Health and Human Services lead with $1.4B and $1.2B respectively, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $546M and Department of State at $388M. On the vendor side, DELOITTE CONSULTING LLP and LMI CONSULTING, LLC are the top two contractors with $399M and $237M respectively. This snapshot is a fiscal year to date picture of contracting activity, not a full-year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the current market size and trend for NAICS 541611?",
        "body": "The market size for FY2026 to date is $5.6B in obligations. Obligations fell 50.2% year over year. Average award size is $592K across 9,506 awards. FY26 to date follows FY25 at $11.3B and earlier annual totals ranging from $12.9B to $15B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 to date spending?",
        "body": "Department of Defense and Department of Health and Human Services are the largest buyers at $1.4B and $1.2B respectively. Department of Homeland Security and Department of State follow at $546M and $388M. The top vendors are DELOITTE CONSULTING LLP at $399M and LMI CONSULTING, LLC at $237M."
      }
    ]
